<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Aimone, Duke of Aosta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tomislav II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Aimone, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aosta">Aosta</a>, was a member of the Italian royal house of Savoy and an admiral. In May 1941 he was designated King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> as Tomislav II under the agreements between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the Independent State of Croatia, but he never went to Croatia and abdicated in 1943. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-aimone-duke-of-aosta.jpg" alt="Prince Aimone, Duke of Aosta" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vanzanten, edited by F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prince_Aimone_of_Savoy_-_restored.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
